- namespace_command

' Publication between two worlds, as pure rules over the namespace. A world
' publishes the names beneath a root record, /<self>/our/<peer>. The reader
' holds them at its mount, /<self>/her/<publisher>, and keeps where the mount
' stands on a card of its own. Nothing here does I/O: a foot carries the
' epics these rules make and admits the writes they plan as one event.
+ net
  + stamp
    ' The version a world publishes: its rift and its case as one number. A
    ' restore raises the rift, so no published version is ever reused, and a
    ' newer continuity always compares greater than an older one. A reference
    ' pinned to a stamp therefore names one content for ever.
    \ rift=nat case=nat
    ^ nat
    | add (mul rift 4294967296) case
  + entry
    ' One name of an epic: its path beneath the root, the version of its
    ' record, the publisher's signature over that moment (0: unsigned), the
    ' content hash of the record (0: the name is gone), and the record. An
    ' epic travels as its entries without their records; each record follows
    ' by its hash, and one the reader already holds is not sent at all.
    : rel=path stamp=nat sig=nat hash=nat record=maybe[myth]
  + put
    ' An entry for a record, unsigned.
    \ rel=path stamp=nat record=myth
    ^ net/entry
    | net/entry rel stamp 0 (net/content record) (./some record)
  + drop
    ' An entry for a name that is gone.
    \ rel=path
    ^ net/entry
    = absent=maybe[myth] .none
    | net/entry rel 0 0 0 absent
  + epic
    ' A consistent change of one published root, from its version base (0:
    ' from nothing) to its version head, under the publisher's signature
    ' over all of it (0: unsigned).
    : base=nat head=nat sig=nat entries=row[net/entry]
  + respell
    ' A record as its publisher sends it. A pinned reference to one of the
    ' publisher's own names carries the published version in place of the
    ' local case, so it names the same content in every world.
    \ self=iota rift=nat record=myth
    ^ myth
    | record.tap.fold record
      \ out [slot value]
      ? value
       > target=safe
        ? (eq target.ver 0) out
        ? (eq target.path.len 0) out
        ? !(reference_index/segment_is target.path.at(0) self) out
        | out.put(slot (safe (net/stamp rift target.ver) target.care target.path))
      out
  + puts
    ' The names of after that are new or changed since before.
    \ self=iota rift=nat before=axal[saga] after=axal[saga]
    ^ row[net/entry]
    = none=row[net/entry] []
    | after.tap.fold none
      \ out [rel now]
      = case now.aeon.yuga.x.data
        same
          ?> (./some then) before.get(rel) .false
          | eq then.aeon.yuga.x.data case
      ? same out
      = sent (net/respell self rift (unpin now.myth))
      | out.snoc((net/put rel (net/stamp rift case) sent))
  + gone
    ' The names of before that after no longer has.
    \ before=axal[saga] after=axal[saga]
    ^ row[net/entry]
    = none=row[net/entry] []
    | before.tap.fold none
      \ out [rel then]
      ? (maybe/is_some after.get(rel)) out
      | out.snoc((net/drop rel))
  + delta
    ' What changed beneath a published root between its z cases k and n; k = 0
    ' asks for everything. None when either case cannot be answered exactly.
    ' The reader then asks for everything, so a wrong or partial answer is
    ' never given in place of a missing one.
    \ rift=nat root=path k=nat n=nat state=namespace
    ^ maybe[net/epic]
    ? !(lt k n) .none
    = history state.local
      empty (axal/new[saga] .none)
    ?> (./some now) (namespace/epoch .z (./some n) root history) .none
    = after | namespace/records now root history
    ? (eq k 0)
      | ./some (net/epic 0 (net/stamp rift n) 0 (net/puts state.self rift empty after))
    ?> (./some then) (namespace/epoch .z (./some k) root history) .none
    = before | namespace/records then root history
      changed | net/puts state.self rift before after
    | ./some (net/epic (net/stamp rift k) (net/stamp rift n) 0 changed.weld((net/gone before after)))
  + content
    ' The content hash of a record: the hash of its pin.
    \ record=myth
    ^ nat
    | PinHash (pin record)
  + word
    ' What a moment's signature is made over. A moment says: this name of
    ' this world, at this version, is this content. It is hashed as a plain
    ' tuple, so the same statement is the same bytes in every world.
    \ world=iota name=path version=nat hash=nat
    ^ nat
    = said=[w=iota n=path v=nat h=nat] [world name version hash]
    | PinHash (pin said)
  + bill
    ' What an epic lists, without the records: each name, its version and
    ' its content hash, 0 when the name is gone.
    \ entries=row[net/entry]
    ^ row[[rel=path stamp=nat hash=nat]]
    | entries.map
      \ item=net/entry
      ^ [rel=path stamp=nat hash=nat]
      [item.rel item.stamp item.hash]
  + heading
    ' What an epic's signature is made over: whose root, from which version
    ' to which, and its bill. So removals and the head are signed too.
    \ root=path base=nat head=nat entries=row[net/entry]
    ^ nat
    = said=[r=path b=nat h=nat e=row[[rel=path stamp=nat hash=nat]]] [root base head (net/bill entries)]
    | PinHash (pin said)
  + seal
    ' Sign an epic as its publisher: each record's moment, then the whole.
    ' The seed is the publisher's signing key and is held by its foot; it
    ' is never a record.
    \ seed=nat root=path epic=net/epic
    ^ net/epic
    = world root.at(0)
      signed
        | epic.entries.map
          \ item=net/entry
          ^ net/entry
          ? (eq 0 item.hash) item
          = said (net/word world root.weld(item.rel) item.stamp item.hash)
          | item.set_sig((Ed25519Sign seed said))
    | net/epic epic.base epic.head (Ed25519Sign seed (net/heading root epic.base epic.head signed)) signed
  + stated
    ' Whether the holder of a key said that a name, at a version, is the
    ' content with this hash.
    \ key=nat name=path said=oath hash=nat
    ^ bool
    ? (eq 0 said.sig) .false
    | eq 1 (Ed25519Verify key (net/word name.at(0) name said.version hash) said.sig)
  + attested
    ' Whether a record, at the version its header states, is what the
    ' holder of a key said of a name. Anyone holding the record, its
    ' header and the key can check it; the publisher need not be asked.
    \ key=nat name=path said=oath record=myth
    ^ bool
    | net/stated key name said (net/content record)
  + proven
    ' Whether an epic is its publisher's: the whole, each moment in it, and
    ' each record that has arrived against the hash its moment names.
    \ key=nat root=path epic=net/epic
    ^ bool
    ? !(eq 1 (Ed25519Verify key (net/heading root epic.base epic.head epic.entries) epic.sig)) .false
    | epic.entries.all
      \ item=net/entry
      ^ bool
      ? (eq 0 item.hash) (maybe/is_none item.record)
      ? !(net/stated key root.weld(item.rel) (oath item.sig item.stamp) item.hash) .false
      ?> (./some record) item.record .true
      | eq item.hash (net/content record)
  + held
    ' A number kept on a record; 0 when there is none.
    \ slot=path name=path state=namespace
    ^ nat
    | (sovereign_care .x name state).fil.fall(myth/new).nat_at(slot 0)
  + key
    ' The key a publisher signs with, as the reader holds it: on the card
    ' of the mount, or, for a second root of the same publisher (its public
    ' one), on the publisher's own card above it, /<self>/io/mesa/<publisher>.
    ' 0 when no key is held: a stranger.
    \ card=path state=namespace
    ^ nat
    = own | net/held ['key] card state
    ? !(eq 0 own) own
    ? (le card.len 4) 0
    | net/held ['key] card.take(4) state
  + forked
    ' Whether the reader holds proof that a publisher's custody signed two
    ' futures (pass/turn). Nothing is believed of such a name.
    \ card=path state=namespace
    ^ bool
    ? (gt (net/held ['fork] card state) 0) .true
    ? (le card.len 4) .false
    | gt (net/held ['fork] card.take(4) state) 0
  + said
    ' The publisher's statement on a held record's current version: zero
    ' when the name holds none.
    \ name=path state=namespace
    ^ oath
    = none (oath 0 0)
    ?> (./known records) (namespace/page .x .none name state) none
    ?> (./some record) records.fil none
    | record.aeon.oath
  + version
    ' The publisher's version a held record stands at; 0 when not held.
    \ name=path state=namespace
    ^ nat
    | (net/said name state).version
  + live
    \ name=path state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | maybe/is_some (sovereign_care .x name state).fil
  + above
    ' The kernel lets nothing live beneath a name that held a record and
    ' holds none. Within one continuity a publisher obeys the same law, so
    ' this never fires. After a restore the publisher's history is another
    ' one: where it lands beneath a name it has no record at and this world
    ' removed one, the name is made again, empty.
    \ mount=path rel=path made=axal[myth] state=namespace out=row[[p=path q=writ]]
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    % k=nat 0
      acc=row[[p=path q=writ]] out
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    ? (ge k rel.len) acc
    = name=path rel.take(k)
      target=path mount.weld(name)
    ? (maybe/is_some made.dip(name).fil) (_ k.inc acc)
    ? (net/live target state) (_ k.inc acc)
    ? !(maybe/is_some state.case(.x target)) (_ k.inc acc)
    ? (acc.any((\ [at wit] (equal[path] at target)))) (_ k.inc acc)
    | _ k.inc acc.snoc([target (writ/make myth/new)])
  + land
    ' The writes that bring a mount from one epic of its publisher, with the
    ' head it then stands at, as one event. Each record is kept exactly as
    ' published; the publisher's version and signature go in its version
    ' header, not in the record. The card holds the publisher's key: an
    ' epic from a world whose key is not held, or one that key did not
    ' sign, is refused. Refused whole too when the epic is
    ' not newer than what is held (a repeat or a regression) or does not
    ' start where the mount stands. A record held at its version or a later
    ' one is left alone and a name already gone is not removed again, so
    ' nothing lands twice and no version goes back. An epic of everything
    ' also removes what the publisher no longer has. A mount mirrors one
    ' published root: a name the kernel spells into another root (the
    ' public one beneath a pairwise mount) is neither written nor removed.
    \ mount=path card=path epic=net/epic state=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    = have | net/held ['head] card state
    ? (le epic.head have) (./err 'net_stale)
    ? !((eq epic.base 0) || (eq epic.base have)) (./err 'net_gap)
    = root=path (reference_index/canonical state.self mount)
      inside (\ rel=path (pith_prefix root (reference_index/canonical state.self mount.weld(rel))))
    ? (epic.entries.any((\ item=net/entry !(inside item.rel)))) (./err 'net_outside)
    = key | net/key card state
    ? (eq 0 key) (./err 'net_stranger)
    ? (net/forked card state) (./err 'net_forked)
    ? !(net/proven key root epic) (./err 'net_forged)
    ? !(net/whole mount epic state) (./err 'net_missing)
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      cull=writ .cull
      whole (eq epic.base 0)
      made
        | epic.entries.fold (axal/new[myth] .none)
          \ tree=axal[myth] item=net/entry
          ^ axal[myth]
          ? (eq 0 item.hash) tree
          | tree.put(item.rel myth/new)
      moved
        | epic.entries.fold none
          \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] item=net/entry
          ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
          = target=path mount.weld(item.rel)
          ? (eq 0 item.hash)
            ? (net/live target state) out.snoc([target cull])
            out
          ? (le item.stamp (net/version target state)) out
          ?> (./some record) item.record out
          | out.snoc([target (writ/hold record (oath item.sig item.stamp))])
      stale
        ? !whole none
        | (sovereign_peek mount state).tap.fold none
          \ out [rel record]
          ? !(inside rel) out
          = under made.dip(rel)
          ? (maybe/is_some under.fil) out
          ? (gt under.kid.size 0) out.snoc([mount.weld(rel) (writ/make myth/new)])
          | out.snoc([mount.weld(rel) cull])
      bare
        ? !whole none
        | epic.entries.fold none
          \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] item=net/entry
          ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
          ? (eq 0 item.hash) out
          | net/above mount item.rel made state out
      mark=myth (myth/sing ['head] (pails/n epic.head))
      writes moved.weld(stale).weld(bare)
    ? (net/live card state) (./ok writes.snoc([card (writ/poke mark)]))
    | ./ok writes.snoc([card (writ/make mark)])
  + lacks
    ' The content hashes an epic names whose records this world must still
    ' be given: those newer than what the mount holds.
    \ mount=path epic=net/epic state=namespace
    ^ row[nat]
    = none=row[nat] []
    | epic.entries.fold none
      \ out=row[nat] item=net/entry
      ^ row[nat]
      ? (eq 0 item.hash) out
      ? (maybe/is_some item.record) out
      ? (le item.stamp (net/version mount.weld(item.rel) state)) out
      ? (out.any((\ seen=nat (eq seen item.hash)))) out
      | out.snoc(item.hash)
  + whole
    ' Whether every record an epic would land has arrived.
    \ mount=path epic=net/epic state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | eq 0 (net/lacks mount epic state).len
  + given
    ' An epic with a record that arrived put where its hash is named.
    \ hash=nat record=myth epic=net/epic
    ^ net/epic
    | epic.set_entries
      | epic.entries.map
        \ item=net/entry
        ^ net/entry
        ? !(eq item.hash hash) item
        | item.set_record((./some record))
  + bare
    ' An epic as it travels: its entries without their records.
    \ epic=net/epic
    ^ net/epic
    = absent=maybe[myth] .none
    | epic.set_entries
      | epic.entries.map
        \ item=net/entry
        ^ net/entry
        | item.set_record(absent)
  + wired
    ' An epic as it travels: plain rows and no records, so it is the same
    ' bytes whatever kernel made it. Each line is one name: its path, its
    ' version, the signature over that moment, and its content hash.
    \ epic=net/epic
    ^ [base=nat head=nat sig=nat lines=row[[rel=path stamp=nat sig=nat hash=nat]]]
    = lines
        | epic.entries.map
          \ item=net/entry
          ^ [rel=path stamp=nat sig=nat hash=nat]
          [item.rel item.stamp item.sig item.hash]
    [epic.base epic.head epic.sig lines]
  + read
    ' An epic from a value that arrived. Nothing is assumed of the value:
    ' none unless it is an epic's travelling form to the last nat.
    \ value=any
    ^ maybe[net/epic]
    = none=maybe[net/epic] .none
      absent=maybe[myth] .none
    ?> (./some sent) (fit[[base=nat head=nat sig=nat lines=row[[rel=path stamp=nat sig=nat hash=nat]]]] value) none
    = [base head signed lines] sent
      entries
        | lines.map
          \ [rel stamp sig hash]
          ^ net/entry
          | net/entry rel stamp sig hash absent
    | ./some (net/epic base head signed entries)
  + shaped
    ' The number of slots of a well-formed myth whose slots all lie between
    ' two bounds; none when the tree is not one the kernel would have built:
    ' a slot out of order, or a count that does not add up.
    \ lo=maybe[path] hi=maybe[path] tree=mop[path pail lt_pith]
    ^ maybe[nat]
    > n=mop/node[path pail lt_pith] tree
     | ./some 0
    = none=maybe[nat] .none
      mid=maybe[path] (./some n.key)
      below
        ?> (./some bound) lo .true
        | lt_pith bound n.key
      above
        ?> (./some bound) hi .true
        | lt_pith n.key bound
    ? !(and below above) none
    ?> (./some left) (net/shaped lo mid n.l) none
    ?> (./some right) (net/shaped mid hi n.r) none
    ? !(eq n.sz left.inc.add(right)) none
    | ./some n.sz
  + sound
    ' A record from a value that arrived. Nothing is assumed of the value:
    ' its representation is checked to any depth, its slots must be in
    ' order, and a slot the kernel would read as a reference must be a whole
    ' reference. What another slot's value holds is its reader's to check;
    ' no value that arrives holds code (the runtime refuses a stream with a
    ' law in it).
    \ value=any
    ^ maybe[myth]
    = none=maybe[myth] .none
      open=maybe[path] .none
    ?> (./some record) (fit[myth] value) none
    ? (maybe/is_none (net/shaped open open record)) none
    = whole
        | record.tap.all
          \ entry
          ?> target=safe entry.val .true
          | maybe/is_some (fit[safe] entry.val)
    ? whole (./some record)
    none
  + shown
    ' A record shown to a world it was not published to: its name as its
    ' publisher spells it, the publisher's statement on that version, and
    ' the record. It is an ordinary value, so it travels inside whatever
    ' record shows it. Whoever holds the publisher's key checks it without
    ' asking the publisher, or the one who showed it, anything.
    : name=path said=oath record=pin[myth]
  + show
    ' What this world holds of a publisher's name, as something to show.
    ' None when the name is not held, or holds no statement of its
    ' publisher.
    \ name=path state=namespace
    ^ maybe[net/shown]
    = none=maybe[net/shown] .none
    ?> (./known records) (namespace/page .x .none name state) none
    ?> (./some held) records.fil none
    ? (eq 0 held.aeon.oath.sig) none
    | ./some (net/shown (reference_index/canonical state.self name) held.aeon.oath held.myth)
  + seen
    ' The record a value shows, when it is a shown record and the holder
    ' of a key said it. Nothing is assumed of the value.
    \ key=nat value=any
    ^ maybe[net/shown]
    = none=maybe[net/shown] .none
    ?> (./some item) (fit[net/shown] value) none
    ? !(net/attested key item.name item.said (unpin item.record)) none
    | ./some item
  + refuse
    ' A landing the kernel refused: the head and the reason, kept where the
    ' mount's standing is kept. The mount is left exactly as it was, and a
    ' later epic lands from where it stands.
    \ card=path head=nat why=iota state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = note=myth (myth/sing ['refused] (pails/n head)).put(['why] (pails/q why))
    ? (net/live card state) [[card (writ/poke note)]]
    | [[card (writ/make note)]]
  + wants
    ' Whether to ask for a head a publisher hints at: only one past what is
    ' held and past what was refused. A hint is compared, never believed.
    \ card=path head=nat state=namespace
    ^ bool
    ? (le head (net/held ['head] card state)) .false
    | gt head (net/held ['refused] card state)
  + serving
    ' A world may serve only while it holds everything it announced. mark is
    ' the highest epoch it announced, kept outside the saved world and
    ' compared at boot. Behind it, the world was restored: its rift is raised
    ' before one version is published again. A foot hears of an epoch only
    ' after the store has saved it, so a crash alone never loses one.
    \ mark=nat state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | ge state.local.top mark
  + ahead
    ' A reader asks from the version it holds. One this world has not made
    ' yet was made by a tree this world no longer has.
    \ rift=nat root=path from=nat state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | gt from (net/stamp rift state.case(.z root).fall(0))
